cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Settling Conjectures 10.1, 10.2 and 10.3 on alternating plane graphs
message: >-
  If you use this software or its certificates, please cite it, and cite the
  paper whose conjectures it settles.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hanyu
    family-names: Yang
    email: hanyu.yang.92@gmail.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0419-4070
repository-code: https://github.com/SeverinVisionary/alternating-plane-graphs
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-02
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked settlement of three of the four open problems in Section 10 of
  Althofer, Haugland, Scherer, Schneider and Van Cleemput, "Alternating plane
  graphs". Conjecture 10.2 is settled by 26 verified certificates together with
  a proved periodic capping lemma that generates a (3,4,5)-alternating plane
  graph at order 48 and every order at least 50. Conjecture 10.3 is settled by a
  3-connected witness at every order from 19 up. Conjecture 10.1 is proved,
  unconditionally: the definition is ambiguous at a bridge, and a counterexample
  is shown to be bridgeless under either reading. The asymptotic degree
  distribution is left open. This work was produced with substantial AI assistance,
  disclosed in AI_DISCLOSURE.md; no AI system is an author.
keywords:
  - alternating plane graphs
  - plane graphs
  - rotation systems
  - combinatorics
  - computer-assisted proof
  - certificate verification
